# editing snapshots of the hindcast notebook and its headless .py mirror.
# Written automatically before an edit, named for the edit that followed
# (.prepatch, .preswitch, .prescenario, ...). Rollback points only -- nothing
# in the pipeline reads them, and the notebook itself is the source of truth.
*.bak
*.prev
*.prepatch
*.preswitch
*.prescenario
*.preoutput

# The test suite. ONE fixture is excluded, not the directory.
#
# This was a bare `tests/`, aimed at the 21.9 MB
# 4-B3D_Rave_pt45_Natural_high.npz -- and it took the tests with it: 0 of the
# 17 files here were tracked, while noxfile.py declares lint / test /
# test-notebooks sessions and setup.cfg carries the flake8 config. A fresh
# clone could not run `nox -s test` because the suite was not in the clone.
# Everything in tests/ except that one file totals 0.8 MB.
tests/4-B3D_Rave_pt45_Natural_high.npz
# The small .npy/.npz fixtures back in past the global rules above, which exist
# for the init domain arrays and the run pickles, not for these.
!tests/**/*.npy
!tests/**/*.npz
tests/4-B3D_Rave_pt45_Natural_high.npz
# CASCADE run outputs: the bulk artifacts only.
# A run directory is ~160 MB, almost all of it the .npz model pickle, and the
# hindcast is run as a 12-scenario matrix. The small text products ARE tracked
# -- the rate CSV, the road summary, the run metadata, and run_index.csv are
# what the comparison figures and the cross-run index read. The .npz and the
# animations are regenerable from those plus the code.
#
# Runs are filed under output/raw_runs/[<forcing arm>/]<start>_<end>/, the arm
# component being absent for the calibration arm. Because output/ is ignored
# wholesale above, that first level has to be re-included.
#
# IT IS RE-INCLUDED AS *, NOT AS THE PERIOD PATTERN. This was
# `[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]_[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/`, which matches a period
# directory and nothing else -- so when forcing arms arrived on 2026-09-01 the
# arm trees fell through to the line above and were ignored whole: 0 tracked
# files under waveHs3/ against 722 under 1984_2004/. run_index.csv IS tracked,
# so a fresh clone got seven index rows naming directories it did not have.
# An arm name comes from HAT_ARM_TAG and cannot be enumerated here, and the
# file-type rules below already keep the bulk out at any depth, so the level is
# re-included as a whole. The dirs the narrow pattern guarded against
# (groin_testing/, wrong/) no longer exist.
output/raw_runs/*
!output/raw_runs/*/
# Every retired index too, not just the live one: they are a few KB each and
# they are the provenance of each index mutation -- the 2026-09-01 arm backfill
# is only checkable against run_index_archive_20260901_235731.csv.
!output/raw_runs/run_index*.csv
output/raw_runs/**/*.npz
output/raw_runs/**/*.gif
output/raw_runs/**/*.png

# ...but NOT the shoreline matrix. The global *.npy rule above exists for the
# init domain arrays; this one is ~19 KB and is the paired baseline that the
# groin extent check (12.3) and the difference GIFs read by run name. Ignoring
# it would mean a fresh clone cannot evaluate a groin run without first
# re-running its no-groin twin.
!output/raw_runs/**/*_shoreline_matrix.npy
